WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.390
Hey friends, so this is going to be a

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:02.870
quick start guide. If in case you

00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:04.710
haven't set up your workspace yet with

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.350
Cloud Code. As you may have seen in a

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.350
lot of our videos here in the classroom,

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:10.510
my preferred way to use Cloud Code is

00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:12.030
through an IDE, an integrated

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.950
development environment, and the one

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:16.510
that I'm using is VS Code. And VS Code

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.230
is open source, meaning it's free, and

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:19.630
you can just download that. And once you

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:21.350
install it, to get Cloud Code, all you

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.070
need to do is to go to the extensions

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.190
tab here at the left. Go and find Cloud

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:27.550
Code, the one from Entropic, and just go

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.230
ahead and install that. And once you

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:31.390
have that installed, now have this Cloud

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:33.470
Code icon here at the left sidebar. But

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.230
if in case you do not see that, all you

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:37.150
need to do is to do a right click here

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.030
on the left sidebar, and just find Cloud

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:41.030
Code in there, and that will toggle the

00:00:41.040 --> 00:00:43.030
visibility of that icon in there. And

00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.550
this is now going to be sort of familiar

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.070
to you if you have used the Cloud

00:00:46.080 --> 00:00:49.310
desktop app or any ChatGPT style chat

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.270
apps from before, because here you can

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.630
just start a new session and just start

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.070
chatting with Cloud Code. Now, before

00:00:55.080 --> 00:00:56.710
you go and talk to Cloud Code, what I

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:58.030
would recommend is to just go to the

00:00:58.040 --> 00:01:00.310
explorer tab and actually open a folder

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:02.510
in here. And you can choose any folder,

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:03.790
but if you're starting for the very

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.990
first time, what I do suggest is to just

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:07.990
choose an empty folder in your device.

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.670
So you can see here, I have this folder

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:11.270
called my workspace, so I'll just go

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:12.750
ahead and select that. And what's now

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:14.630
going to happen is that this explorer

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:16.750
tab on the left will display all of the

00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.510
files that are in that folder. Now,

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:20.310
obviously because that is an empty

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.110
folder, then there is nothing here. And

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:24.150
right now this folder is empty, but as

00:01:24.160 --> 00:01:25.990
we continue on throughout the course, we

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:28.350
will actually fill this up with your own

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.310
personal context and all of the tools

00:01:30.320 --> 00:01:32.190
and the output that Cloud Code creates

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:33.710
that will now be stored within this

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.550
folder. And as you progress through the

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:37.830
course, this will effectively be your

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.310
own operating system or second brain,

00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:42.270
and where as you use Cloud Code more and

00:01:42.280 --> 00:01:45.230
more as a teammate or as a fleet of AI

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.830
agents, then this workspace that you

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.470
have chosen, this folder, is now going

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.870
to evolve to contain all the documents

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.630
of your current business, including all

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.550
the bills, the outputs, the connections,

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:56.470
the tools that we will go through in

00:01:56.480 --> 00:01:58.550
this course. But first and foremost, for

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:00.030
you to set up some of the essential

00:02:00.040 --> 00:02:01.750
files of CloudCode in here, what you can

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.310
do is to go to CloudCode, start a new

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:05.830
session in here, and just go ahead and

00:02:05.840 --> 00:02:08.150
type in {slash} init. And what that is

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.910
going to do is that's just going to

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.670
initialize CloudCode's startup sequence,

00:02:12.680 --> 00:02:14.990
actually look at your current workspace.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.710
So, let's say you linked it to a folder

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.190
with some business documents that you

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:20.110
already have, then it will actually look

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.710
through those files and give you an

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:23.790
overview and recommendation of how to

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.150
set it up properly. I think with

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:26.710
CloudCode, if in case you haven't used

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:28.270
any agentic platform before, is that

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:30.350
they are sort of verbose. So, you can

00:02:30.360 --> 00:02:32.110
see here it provides you a duration of

00:02:32.120 --> 00:02:33.830
how long they thought. It gives you an

00:02:33.840 --> 00:02:35.630
update on what it's doing at the moment.

00:02:35.640 --> 00:02:38.230
It uses these commands called bash and

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:40.190
glob, which you don't necessarily need

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:42.030
to understand because a lot of that

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.750
technical heavy lifting is being handled

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:45.430
by CloudCode anyway, but essentially

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.190
those are just what we call terminal

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.510
commands in order for CloudCode to work

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.910
with your files. So, things like

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:53.070
analyzing and reading your files or even

00:02:53.080 --> 00:02:55.470
moving your files if we so desire. So,

00:02:55.480 --> 00:02:57.030
bottom line, it now tells me that my

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:59.350
workspace, this folder that I chose, is

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:00.870
completely empty. And so, what's going

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.509
to happen now is that it's going to ask

00:03:02.519 --> 00:03:04.390
you a couple of questions on how you

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.590
want to set up this project. And from

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.470
here, you can literally just give it any

00:03:08.480 --> 00:03:10.190
inputs on the context of what you're

00:03:10.200 --> 00:03:11.710
trying to do, and also provide it some

00:03:11.720 --> 00:03:13.590
information on your business or your

00:03:13.600 --> 00:03:16.070
work in order for it to create a

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:17.910
cloud.md. Now, in case you're just

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.870
following along for now and just want to

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.790
get started as quick as possible, what

00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:23.670
you can do at the moment is just have it

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:25.550
to create the default files and folders

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.509
for now, send ahead that prompt, and it

00:03:27.519 --> 00:03:28.910
will just set up your workspace.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.790
Basically, that whole folder with all of

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:32.229
the essential files that we will go

00:03:32.239 --> 00:03:33.670
through in this course, which includes

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.949
standard folders including a cloud.md,

00:03:35.959 --> 00:03:37.509
which we will explore a bit more, a

00:03:37.519 --> 00:03:39.949
readme file in this .gitignore. So, the

00:03:39.959 --> 00:03:41.830
reason why this works is because even if

00:03:41.840 --> 00:03:43.870
it creates files for us right now, we

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:45.509
can actually really easily edit this

00:03:45.519 --> 00:03:47.949
later on because CloudCode is really,

00:03:47.959 --> 00:03:50.150
really quick when it comes to editing

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.230
these files for you. And once it is

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:54.310
done, if you go back to your Explorer

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:56.070
page, you will now see that you have

00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:58.230
different folders and files in here. And

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.110
just for avoidance of doubt, this whole

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.830
Explorer page at the left, if you do a

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:03.830
right click and click on reveal in File

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:05.550
Explorer, what that will do is it just

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:08.070
show and open this File Explorer of

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.150
yours. And here you can literally see

00:04:10.160 --> 00:04:12.470
that these are files that are existing

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:14.110
in your computer. So right now there's

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.830
not a lot of files in here, but as I

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:17.590
have said, once you start using Cloud

00:04:17.600 --> 00:04:19.229
Code more and more, this is going to be

00:04:19.239 --> 00:04:21.590
filling up with a lot of your context,

00:04:21.600 --> 00:04:23.550
which Cloud Code can use in order to

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:25.270
drive results for you. Now, one very

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:27.430
important file across this workspace is

00:04:27.440 --> 00:04:30.270
this cloud.md. And that is a specific

00:04:30.280 --> 00:04:32.310
file that Cloud Code actually looks for

00:04:32.320 --> 00:04:34.150
every time you open a new session and

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:36.190
chat with it. So, just to give one quick

00:04:36.200 --> 00:04:38.350
example, if you open that file and

00:04:38.360 --> 00:04:39.790
actually give an edit here, let's say

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:42.390
I'll give it a context that my name is

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:44.630
Jay, and I add in, for example, I live

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:47.030
in Sydney. And if we hit control S so

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.070
that we can save that file, if we now

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.510
open Cloud Code, which by the way you

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:52.510
can also access through this icon, and

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:54.310
if we ask it, "What's my name and where

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:56.070
do I live?" If you fire that off,

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:57.830
normally a chatbot doesn't have

00:04:57.840 --> 00:04:59.909
knowledge of that. But because you added

00:04:59.919 --> 00:05:02.270
that context into your cloud.md, every

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:04.350
Cloud Code session actually begins by

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:06.670
pre-injecting this whole text file into

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:08.350
this session, which includes that piece

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:10.430
of text that we included in this file.

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.230
So, this is going to be a concept that

00:05:12.240 --> 00:05:14.070
we will explore more and more throughout

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.310
this master class. But for now, what is

00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:17.870
important is that you can access Cloud

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.670
Code by starting a new session here, and

00:05:19.680 --> 00:05:21.710
that you are able to operate VS Code

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:23.630
properly by having this knowledge that

00:05:23.640 --> 00:05:25.470
if you open up multiple tabs, you can

00:05:25.480 --> 00:05:27.750
actually drag and drop these windows so

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.070
that you can concurrently run and

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:31.990
preview files wherever that you want to

00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:33.390
place them, which is going to be a

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:36.030
powerful feature for you once you start

00:05:36.040 --> 00:05:38.470
operating multiple agents at the same

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.880
time.
